{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 107, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 2's only input path is edge 1, so a 3x3 conv there carries most of the cell's learnable computation."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op with a 3x3 conv adds far more capacity than replacing a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is already absent, removing edge 4 leaves only the direct edge 3 into the output, collapsing the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 3 leaves edge 4 as the sole path to the output, severely reducing depth and connectivity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge 3, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 4 feeding the output, which is far more damaging than when edge 3 provides a bypass."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is none, removing edge 0 disconnects both intermediate nodes from the input, leaving only edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-output edge, the path through edge 2 is a main route, so removing it hurts much more."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1 is none, edge 2 is node 2's only input, so removing it kills node 2 and makes edge 5 useless."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a learnable 3x3 conv for pooling loses capacity, unlike swapping a skip or none for pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no edge creates a new deep path to the output, whereas replacing an existing op gains less."}], "tok": 17700, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "none"]], [["none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "none"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [1, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "avg_pool_3